                        "glosses": [
                            "To misunderstand something; to disregard or fail to pay attention."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecab6722-c049-4911-9241-13b6e79af76e",
                                "sense_id": "96cef61b-7d2d-3086-947c-7a54186817bc",
                                "text": "I would have cabled you to withdraw it from the Century, but I didn't, for I was sure I could depend upon Gilder's declining it. If he hasn't done it, please take it away from him and charge him with being drunk and misattending to his duties."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2260f59e-b61f-4f43-a759-4b904ff639b6",
                                "sense_id": "96cef61b-7d2d-3086-947c-7a54186817bc",
                                "text": "They ſhall recover the miſattended vvords of Chriſt to the ſincerity of their true ſenſe from manifold contradictions, and ſhall open them vvith the key of charity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1a17cb4-6302-43b7-86da-2bd5bc0e64ca",
                                "sense_id": "96cef61b-7d2d-3086-947c-7a54186817bc",
                                "text": "Then how do you account for Mr. Goffin stating that he gave a lesson on Thursday as usual ? — I did not hear the lesson. I must have been misattending if he did give one, because we were all changing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ad3218f-fe38-442d-a663-dcf93f8d70f3",
                                "sense_id": "96cef61b-7d2d-3086-947c-7a54186817bc",
                                "text": "From the bottom-up view, the reader with attention deficits may misattend to the salient features of words."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e57de9f-9125-4cf4-ae50-ac520038dcbd",
                                "sense_id": "96cef61b-7d2d-3086-947c-7a54186817bc",
                                "text": "It is a case of 'epistemic drift' as defined by Kemeny (1999), in which discourses without firm disciplinary roots tend to misattend to facts and jump to misleading conclusions."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e3a7c7c-d150-3a66-8898-1fd1dbedc480",
                        "entry_id": "2cf73a8e-1f4e-371e-a400-cf23b5b9907d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fail to look after properly."
